# The sacrifice may be a creature (CR 701.21a) and the reflexive trigger's damage may be aimed at an opponent's creature (CR 603.12,
# 120.2b): Bot1 sacrifices its Ornithopter and 2 damage kills Bot2's 0/2 Ornithopter (one damage would not). Only what the
# controller controls is offered, so Bot2's Ornithopter is not a legal sacrifice.

[Bot1 Deck]
Boilerbilges Ripper
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Ornithopter
Mountain
Mountain x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Boilerbilges Ripper.Cast
? Bot1.Mana =
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Choose(Boilerbilges Ripper)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Boilerbilges Ripper.Power = 4
